\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Thee will I praise with all my heart,
\par And tell mankind how good Thou art,
\par How marvellous Thy works of grace;
\par Thy name I will in songs record,
\par And joy and glory in my Lord,
\par Extolled above all thanks and praise.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. The Lord will save His people here;
\par In times of need their help is near
\par To all by sin and hell oppressed;
\par And they that know Thy name will trust
\par In Thee, who, to Thy promise just,
\par Hast never left a soul distressed.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. The Lord is by His judgements known;
\par He helps His poor afflicted one,
\par His sorrows all He bears in mind;
\par The mourner shall not always weep,
\par Who sows in tears in joy shall reap,
\par With grief who seeks with joy shall find.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. A helpless soul that looks to Thee
\par Is sure at last Thy face to see,
\par And all Thy goodness to partake;
\par The sinner who for Thee doth grieve,
\par And longs, and labours to believe,
\par Thou never, never wilt forsake.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

